Short:        One pack: AmigaOS 3.2.3, ready to use
Uploader:     (We fill this in at upload time)
Author:       AmigaChrome Team
Type:         util/misc
Version:      0.6.1
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 3.2.0
Distribution: Aminet

OpenUp sets up an AmigaOS 3.2.3 installation in one go. Install AmigaOS 3.2.3,
run OpenUp, reboot: graphics on every monitor, networking, MUI programs,
printing, mail, archives and file types all work, with nothing more to read.

It finds what it is running on (a real Amiga with its cards, a PiStorm, or
AmigaChrome) and installs the Open family to match. Anything it replaces is
kept, and one uninstaller puts everything back.

Version 0.6 is for AmigaChrome instances. Its Installer installs, as you
choose:
- OpenSocket: the network, through the PC (bsdsocket.library 4.2);
- OpenPrint and OpenView: printing to PDF and network printers, and viewing;
- AmigaChrome sharing: the clipboard and files, shared with the PC;
- OpenLook: one look for every GadTools program, title bars and borders too
  (Open, Graphite, Ember, Clear or Classic), with a clear screen font and a
  little more room in the title bars; Look in SYS:Prefs changes it (dark by
  the clock, accent, Lite for a real 68040, desktop profiles);
- Backgrounds: the look's desktop as Workbench's backdrop, for your screen;
- OpenTypes: which program opens each kind of file (SYS:Prefs/OpenTypes);
- OpenCompress: opens, tests and extracts ADF, ADZ, DMS, LhA, zip, tar and
  gzip, from its window in SYS:Utilities or from the Shell;
- OpenService: services from AmigaChrome's boards and from a Cradle you pair
  with (DEVS:openservice.device, and C:Nursery to list them); nothing goes on
  the network until a Cradle is paired.
- OpenImage: datatypes for WebP and WebM on the Amiga itself, and through
  OpenService for AVIF, HEIC, JPEG XL, camera RAW, SVG, FLAC, Ogg, MP3, MIDI,
  MP4 and other video, and office documents; datatypes already there stay;
- OpenWindows: windows snap to edges and to each other, Amiga+Tab switches
  between them, the wheel scrolls the window under the pointer, and programs'
  windows open where they were last left (Windows in SYS:Prefs);
- OpenDock: a dock for your programs, starting with ToolManager's, AmiDock's
  or AmiStart's buttons when you have one (Dock in SYS:Prefs);
- OpenUp Setup: a few questions at the next start, and the startup switches;
- OpenRTG (new, off unless picked): Workbench on OpenRTG's own 16-bit screen
  on AmigaChrome's graphics board, without Picasso96, whose monitor for that
  board is put aside and comes back with the uninstaller.
Every file it adds or replaces is listed in ENVARC:OpenAmiga/OpenUp.manifest;
replaced files are kept in SYS:Storage/OpenUp-Superseded; its startup lines
sit in one marked block in S:User-Startup. Uninstall-OpenUp (in
SYS:Utilities/OpenUp) takes it all out again.

